{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q: those parents lie in the answer’s subtree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. So a query is one range minimum over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n − 1 parent positions (the Euler tour reduction on half the entries), answered by 64-entry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"About two words per vertex, plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) for the table.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/lowestcommonancestors"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors","int